| Fine mesh | Mesh 6 8 | 1,635,129 | 85.8% | 20.77 | 1.333 | Passed after mesh-quality fix; converged in 431 iterations; about 80 min |
| Zero-angle check | Earlier mesh, AoA 0 deg | — | — | -0.015 | 0.79 | Near-zero lift as expected for the symmetric wing |
| Later y+ = 30 | Wake box, mesh 5 7, 3 layers | 1,060,448 | 100% | 19.62 | 1.350 | `checkMesh` OK; avg/max y+ 22.3/52.4, rejected for wall-function use |
| Current y+ = 60 baseline | Wake box, mesh 5 7, 3 layers; 600 iterations | 1,060,448 | 100% | 19.42 | 1.459 | `checkMesh` OK; avg/max y+ 39.4/99.3; residual targets not met |
| Current y+ = 60 extended | Same setup; 1200 iterations | 1,060,448 | 100% | 19.42 | 1.459 | `checkMesh` OK; residual targets still not met |
| Aggressive nose-box test | Nose level 8 + wake box | — | — | — | — | Failed before solve: 937 negative-volume cells, max non-orthogonality 179.98939, max skewness 18725.4 |

Other recorded checks and qualifications:

- `pytest -q backend/test_pipeline.py`: 10 passed, 1 skipped.
- A repeated run with the same settings produced bit-identical values; the exact pair of run directories was not recorded.
- One early wake-box attempt did not actually apply the box (cell count stayed 806,197); do not treat that run as a valid wake-box comparison. A later applied wake/tip-box run is listed above.
- Reduced nose refinement was reported as giving no benefit; the aggressive nose-level-8 case failed mesh checks as shown above.
- Mesh 6 8 initially had 8 inside-out cells when the relaxed tetrahedron-quality check was disabled. Setting `minTetQuality` to `1e-30` allowed the recorded 6 8 mesh to pass; mesh 5 8 remains failed.
- The earlier reference was a model-based fully turbulent NACA0012 estimate (lift about 21.5–23.1 N, drag about 1.4–1.5 N), not experimental data. It suggested drag was close and lift low; it is not experimental validation.
